40697,imgsize-110387.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Australian couple bought a cattle farm and planted 34,000 trees to restore rainforest]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133342177.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/australian-couple-bought-a-cattle-farm-and-planted-34000-trees-to-restore-rainforest-for-koalas-and-other-wildlife/articleshow/133342177.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/australian-couple-bought-a-cattle-farm-and-planted-34000-trees-to-restore-rainforest-for-koalas-and-other-wildlife/articleshow/133342177.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T14:13:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133342597,imgsize-1151264.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Netanyahu's party puts Mamdani alongside Iran, Hezbollah leaders on billboard]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133341034.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Israeli Prime Minister Netanyahu's party placed Mayor Mamdani's image on a billboard.  This billboard featured Mamdani alongside leaders hostile to Israel's interests.  Netanyahu is campaigning for re-election amid political challenges in Israel.  He has increasingly used Mamdani's criticism as campaign messaging.  The exchange occurs while Gaza ceasefire efforts remain stalled.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/dont-let-them-win-netanyahus-party-puts-zohran-mamdani-alongside-iran-hezbollah-leaders-on-billboard/articleshow/133341034.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/dont-let-them-win-netanyahus-party-puts-zohran-mamdani-alongside-iran-hezbollah-leaders-on-billboard/articleshow/133341034.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T13:24:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133341400,imgsize-1177681.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Oklahoma woman finds missing dog 1,100 miles away in North Carolina after 2 weeks]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133340715.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/oklahoma-woman-finds-missing-dog-1100-miles-away-in-north-carolina-after-nearly-two-weeks-and-no-one-knows-how-he-got-there/articleshow/133340715.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/oklahoma-woman-finds-missing-dog-1100-miles-away-in-north-carolina-after-nearly-two-weeks-and-no-one-knows-how-he-got-there/articleshow/133340715.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T13:16:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133341264,imgsize-1252154.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Pakistan govt to challenge SC order to move jailed ex-PM Imran Khan to hospital]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133341219.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/pakistan-govt-to-challenge-sc-order-to-move-jailed-ex-pm-imran-khan-to-hospital/articleshow/133341219.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/pakistan-govt-to-challenge-sc-order-to-move-jailed-ex-pm-imran-khan-to-hospital/articleshow/133341219.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T13:10:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133341564,imgsize-281790.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Nature’s biodegradable plastic may hold clues to Earth’s crisis]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133341023.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature-invented-biodegradable-plastic-millions-of-years-ago-and-animals-have-been-eating-it-ever-since-scientists-now-think-it-could-offer-a-clue-to-earths-plastic-crisis/articleshow/133341023.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature-invented-biodegradable-plastic-millions-of-years-ago-and-animals-have-been-eating-it-ever-since-scientists-now-think-it-could-offer-a-clue-to-earths-plastic-crisis/articleshow/133341023.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T13:05:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133341173,imgsize-506923.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[1,300 Swiss villagers face danger as thawing glaciers loosen a massive Alpine rock]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133340644.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Kandersteg village in Switzerland faces a significant landslide threat from an unstable mountain. Scientists link this danger to thawing permafrost and changing glacier dynamics caused by climate change. While the threat is not immediate, authorities have prepared evacuation plans and monitoring systems. Residents are aware of the risks but remain calm, trusting the implemented safety measures. This situation highlights the increasing natural risks faced by mountain communities globally.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/an-unstable-rock-formation-threatens-the-existence-of-an-entire-swiss-village-of-1300-residents-as-thawing-glaciers-destabilise-the-alps/articleshow/133340644.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/an-unstable-rock-formation-threatens-the-existence-of-an-entire-swiss-village-of-1300-residents-as-thawing-glaciers-destabilise-the-alps/articleshow/133340644.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T12:50:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133340809,imgsize-156603.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A rotating 'garbage island' spreads over 1.6 million sq km in the Pacific with 50 kilograms of plastic per square kilometre]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133339710.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Between the shores of Hawaii and California floats a staggering 1.6 million square kilometers of plastic debris. This island of waste includes not just nets and ropes but also countless microplastics that pose serious threats to marine wildlife. Animals often mistake plastics for food, while others become trapped in ghost fishing gear.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/a-rotating-garbage-island-spreads-over-1-6-million-sq-km-in-the-pacific-plastic-averages-50-kilograms-per-square-kilometre-and-75-to-86-of-the-debris-comes-from-fishing-gear/articleshow/133339710.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/a-rotating-garbage-island-spreads-over-1-6-million-sq-km-in-the-pacific-plastic-averages-50-kilograms-per-square-kilometre-and-75-to-86-of-the-debris-comes-from-fishing-gear/articleshow/133339710.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T12:10:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133339733,imgsize-324805.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kansas couple builds tornado-resistant home from tyres, cans and boxes]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133339512.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In an innovative twist on sustainable living, a couple in Kansas is transforming discarded items into a unique residence. This Earthship features around 1,000 tires and 16,000 aluminum cans, built to endure severe weather, including tornadoes and fires. It will autonomously generate power, harvest rainwater, and process wastewater, demonstrating how waste can be creatively repurposed into a haven.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-kansas-couple-is-building-a-tornado-resistant-home-from-1000-tyres-16000-cans-and-1000-cardboard-boxes-construction-begins-this-year/articleshow/133339512.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-kansas-couple-is-building-a-tornado-resistant-home-from-1000-tyres-16000-cans-and-1000-cardboard-boxes-construction-begins-this-year/articleshow/133339512.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T12:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133339666,imgsize-188350.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1993, an art historian found a forgotten painting; 33 years later, its female creator was rediscovered]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133339601.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A remarkable find by an art historian in 1993 ignited a relentless pursuit to recover the lost masterpieces of Michaelina Wautier. This accomplished 17th-century painter's works had long been misattributed to men throughout history. The pivotal recovery of her 'The Five Senses' series in 2020 heralded a new era, culminating in a landmark exhibition at London's Royal Academy in 2026, finally restoring her rightful legacy after centuries in the shadows.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-1993-an-art-historian-spotted-a-forgotten-painting-in-a-museum-storeroom-33-years-later-its-female-creator-was-rediscovered-in-london/articleshow/133339601.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-1993-an-art-historian-spotted-a-forgotten-painting-in-a-museum-storeroom-33-years-later-its-female-creator-was-rediscovered-in-london/articleshow/133339601.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T12:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133339673,imgsize-388935.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Tina Jin, 15-year-old who turned animal bones into a water-cleaning material]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133339290.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-tina-jin-the-15-year-old-massachusetts-student-who-turned-animal-bones-into-a-new-material-for-cleaning-polluted-water/articleshow/133339290.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-tina-jin-the-15-year-old-massachusetts-student-who-turned-animal-bones-into-a-new-material-for-cleaning-polluted-water/articleshow/133339290.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T11:54:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><